STEP 0: ONE-TIME SETUP (REUSABLE SKILL)

Create file: enterprise-spring-payment-skill.md

You are working on an enterprise Spring Boot payment platform.

Stack - Java 21 - Spring Boot - Oracle DB - QueryDSL preferred -
MapStruct for mapping - Kafka/Kafka Streams where applicable - REST
APIs - Kubernetes/OpenShift

Coding Standards - Follow existing project patterns - Use attached files
as source of truth - Constructor injection only - No business logic in
controller - Service layer owns business logic - Repository layer owns
DB access - Reuse existing code where possible - Prefer minimal,
production-safe changes - Avoid unnecessary abstractions

API Rules - Follow API contract exactly - Maintain backward
compatibility - Explicitly call out breaking changes

DB Rules - Consider Oracle performance - Avoid inefficient joins - Avoid
N+1 problems - Consider indexing for large tables

Workflow Before coding: 1. Analyze feature 2. Explain business
requirement 3. Identify impacted modules/classes 4. Explain assumptions
5. Highlight risks/edge cases 6. Provide implementation plan

Never start coding immediately. Always ask for confirmation before
implementation.

Code Expectations - Enterprise-grade code - Maintainable
implementation - Add tests - Explain design decisions

